{"id":"09150f18-4094-415b-bbf4-ca4348569ec4","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"f1f61ba6d1b21d82","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/instance.ts","baseline":{"blob":"efe29108b83a7bacdbb5589b6d598087769b409f","start":1,"end":27},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","PREFIX","=","\"","instance:","\""]},"context":{"after":"add5145de5a001cc"}},"payload":{"text":"An instance of the editor, kept apart from another on the same origin: `?instance=<name>`, so an editor run inside an\neditor's preview window (which is how the editor's own tests come to run in the editor) has its own workspace, its own\nVS Code state and its own settings, and nothing it does reaches the real ones. Same origin means the same IndexedDB and\nlocalStorage, and VS Code names its databases itself, so this works underneath everything: in each realm on the page's\nthread, imported first, IndexedDB's and Storage's methods are wrapped to add the instance to every name.\n\nA frame with the name in its own address is that instance's top: it renders the shell, whatever frame it's in. The\nframes under it find the name by looking up. Workers aren't covered: the only database one opens is BABLR's cache of\nparses, kept by the text's own hash, which instances can safely share. The one service worker serves them all, each by\nits tab. Without a name, nothing here does anything.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:23.493Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:23.493Z"}
{"id":"4179cc0e-918c-4632-8568-860420e07994","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"28448d5778c07242","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/instance.ts","baseline":{"blob":"fedbe59534f773b05ad051004c9e373381845850","start":4975,"end":5374},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","isolateDatabaseNames","(","name",":","string",",","database",":","{","\"","prototype","\"",":","IDBDatabase","}",")",":","void","{","const","stored","=","Object",".","getOwnPropertyDescriptor","(","database",".","prototype",",","\"","name","\"",")","!",".","get","!",";","Object",".","defineProperty","(","database",".","prototype",",","\"","name","\"",",","{","\"","configurable","\"",":","true",",","\"","get","\"",":","function","(","this",":","IDBDatabase",")",":","string","{","const","own","=","stored",".","call","(","this",")","as","string",";","return","ownName","(","name",",","own",")","??","own",";","}","}",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"f9a80a4a56f4bd83","after":"8d6356fd4d70e744"}},"payload":{"text":"A database's `name`, from here on, as `name` asked for it, not as it's stored: zen-fs opens its object store by it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:14.143Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:14.143Z"}
{"id":"47b400ef-0d42-4b19-a56a-5e6812f948e2","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"467eaa43261956b8","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/instance.ts","baseline":{"blob":"fb808efd6aece8fa6243d29b8ffed59fccd01fc1","start":2802,"end":3154},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","seedFiles","(","search",":","string",")",":","Record","<","string",",","string",">","|","undefined","{","const","seed","=","new","URLSearchParams","(","search",")",".","get","(","\"","seed","\"",")",";","if","(","instance","===","undefined","||","seed","===","null",")","{","return","undefined",";","}","return","JSON",".","parse","(","new","TextDecoder","(",")",".","decode","(","Uint8Array",".","from","(","atob","(","seed",")",",","(","character",")","=>","character",".","codePointAt","(","0",")","!",")",")",")","as","Record","<","string",",","string",">",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"595710f6004061a2","after":"f9a80a4a56f4bd83"}},"payload":{"text":"The files an instance starts with, in its address (`&seed=`: base64 of JSON, each path from the workspace's root, with its\ntext), in place of the starter: what a test sets up, with nothing crossing from another instance. Only an instance has\nthem, and what it keeps is written over them.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:16.215Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:55:16.215Z"}
